-- Through a nested let: the residue factor is attached to the inner
-- variable's world in stage 1 (y bound at fst of the sample) and carried
-- over when the y-set is transported onto x in stage 2.
-- p((1.5, 0.3)) = phi(1.5 - 1) * phi(0.3)
p((1.5, 0.3))=(0.1342734258740318, 2.0)
p((-1.0, 0.3)) is impossible
p((1.5, ANY))=(0.3520653267642995, 1.0)
